+    <div style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;">
+      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--accent-light);border-radius:var(--radius-md);padding:16px 20px;">
+        <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;">Is the trust irrevocable?</summary>
+        <p style="margin-top:10px;line-height:1.7;">Yes. The Settlor established the trust as an irrevocable public charitable trust and has relinquished all claim to the corpus fund.</p>
+      </details>
+      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--accent-light);border-radius:var(--radius-md);padding:16px 20px;">
+        <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;">Who is the Managing Trustee?</summary>
+        <p style="margin-top:10px;line-height:1.7;">Shri S. Govindaraj, the Settlor, holds the office of Managing Trustee for his lifetime.</p>
+      </details>
+      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--accent-light);border-radius:var(--radius-md);padding:16px 20px;">
+        <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;">Can trustees or their relatives benefit financially?</summary>
+        <p style="margin-top:10px;line-height:1.7;">No. No part of the trust's income or property may benefit the Settlor, trustees, or their relatives, by way of salary, allowance, profit, or otherwise.</p>
+      </details>
+      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--accent-light);border-radius:var(--radius-md);padding:16px 20px;">
+        <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;">What happens if the trust is dissolved?</summary>
+        <p style="margin-top:10px;line-height:1.7;">Trust funds first settle liabilities; remaining assets go to another trust or association with similar objects, after approval from the Commissioner of Income Tax — never to trustees or their relatives.</p>
